Z||000016||V8Fiero||12-08-2000||12:25 AM||||NO WAY would I wanna work on that engine if I ever had a problem with it. A little too cramped on the engine compartment for me. Doesnt look like it fits very well. Oh yea. I suggest before you do any selling of the so called "kit" that you do alot of R & D. I do hope you know what that is. That is what you are pay probably 80% for when you buy a V8 Kit. You dont only get the kit but you get the knowledge and the expertise to make it work.<P>Again. Not a flame. My .02<P>Thanks.<BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000017||jlruiz67||12-08-2000||12:52 AM||||This is not meant as a Flame.<P>I know that R&D is not cheap but could someone tell me how long does it take to make up for the R&D expenditure and for the price of the products to actually go down? If you invent a new drug you have like 10 years of exclusivity and then the product can be made by others and the price drops dramatically. I know that you can spend lots of money on R&D but how long can you say your getting back your investment. I think that it would be great if some one came out with a inexpensive kit for the masses. I think that it is time for someone to step up to the plate. There are many old, tired Fiero engines in need of re build or replacement and if someone came out with the right product for the masses I think more of us would venture into the engine upgrade world and we would see more powerful fiero's on the streets and I also think that this would be a great business plan. <P><BR>Any one out there. There has been many years and many people with V8 experience R&D has been done so, come on lets have it.<P>I can take the flames to come but please also respond to my question.<BR>Thanks<P>ps. please don't take this as an endorsment of the conversion above, I don't know the details of that conversion so I have to hold on that one but my point stands and hope some can respond.<p>[This message has been edited by jlruiz67 (edited 12-08-2000).]||||reg||5
