Z||000021||KRMFiero||12-08-2000||07:45 AM||||Okay I seriously would love to do this, but i dont have a garage full of everything, so When you come out with this kit, make sure it eather tells us every exact bolt we have to buy (or better yet include them with your kit)    I would hate to buy a engine, buy your kit and then not be able to get it in or not have all the bolts and have my Fiero out of service for weeks<P><BR>btw  would a 1987 Cadillac Sedan Deville 4.5L V8  engine fit?  I'm not sure if it is front or rare wheel drive....<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<BR>Front - AudioBahn 4 x 10<BR>Headrest - AudioBahn 3 1/2<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||bubbajoexx||12-08-2000||06:11 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B>Okay I seriously would love to do this, but i dont have a garage full of everything, so When you come out with this kit, make sure it eather tells us every exact bolt we have to buy (or better yet include them with your kit)    I would hate to buy a engine, buy your kit and then not be able to get it in or not have all the bolts and have my Fiero out of service for weeks<P><BR>btw  would a 1987 Cadillac Sedan Deville 4.5L V8  engine fit?  I'm not sure if it is front or rare wheel drive....<P>Kyle<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>just lift the hood if the motor is transverse mounted it the right one.<p>[This message has been edited by bubbajoexx (edited 12-08-2000).]||||reg||1
